(7283104, 1134001, 24073, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot too, I can''t help to wonder what would of happen in Black and White.  I also think the background is a bit distracting, and within composure, he is standing just a little bit crooked, and I know it doesn''t seem like much, but it shapes the overall image into a little bit of an awkward balance.  Still a good shot, and I like it a lot.<br/> <br/>Subtract the big red/blue thing behind him that I can''t even tell what it is, and center up his face with a little depth in the streets behind him, maybe turn to black and white, and boom this is a top 3 entry.  However, I must say that I am hardly in expert in the field of street photography, but I remember one guy whos name was I think Librodo, and that dude was excellent with these kind of shots, I''ve seen others I just don''t remember their names right off.</td>', 'I liked this shot too, I can''t help to wonder what would of happen in Black and White.  I also think the background is a bit distracting, and within composure, he is standing just a little bit crooked, and I know it doesn''t seem like much, but it shapes the overall image into a little bit of an awkward balance.  Still a good shot, and I like it a lot. Subtract the big red/blue thing behind him that I can''t even tell what it is, and center up his face with a little depth in the streets behind him, maybe turn to black and white, and boom this is a top 3 entry.  However, I must say that I am hardly in expert in the field of street photography, but I remember one guy whos name was I think Librodo, and that dude was excellent with these kind of shots, I''ve seen others I just don''t remember their names right off.', '2014-11-10 08:32:18.000000', NULL, 0),
